# CI/CD & Production Readiness

## Deterministic quality gates

New or modified code must pass without errors or warnings:

- Typecheck: `npx tsc --noEmit`
- Lint: `npm run lint` (`next` ESLint)
- Format consistently (Prettier if present)

Do not leave unused imports, `eslint-disable` without justification, or `@ts-expect-error` without a comment.

## Testable structure

- Keep pure logic in `src/lib/*` so it can be unit-tested (Vitest/Jest) without rendering the full app.
- Hooks should return typed values and accept dependencies (fetchers, clocks) when it helps testing.
- Route Handlers: parse → authorize → call a lib function → map to HTTP. Do not bury business rules inside `route.ts`.

## Zero-warning tolerance

- Do not commit types that only work because of `any` or unchecked `!`.
- If a change would break `next build` (Prisma client, env, Clerk), fix it in the same change.
- Mobile app (`flipon-app`) depends on these APIs — do not ship breaking JSON shapes without updating both sides.
